  "quests": [
    {
      "id": "5E80000000000001",
      "title": "Chapter 5: The LV Factory",
      "icon": {
        "id": "modern_industrialization:lv_steam_turbine",
        "count": 1
      },
      "x": 0.0,
      "y": 0.0,
      "shape": "hexagon",
      "size": 1.25,
      "dependencies": [
        "5E5000000000000A"
      ],
      "description": [
        "You have made the first LV Steam Turbine in Progression Routes: Biology to Electricity. Now turn that bootstrap into a repeatable factory.",
        "The main route builds component automation, an Electric Blast Furnace and your first aluminum. Diamonds and convenience machines are optional branches.",
        "Item tasks detect your inventory without consuming anything. Checkmarks are practical jobs: confirm them after building and testing the described setup. Keep the steam workshop running while you upgrade."
      ],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "5E80000000001010",
          "type": "checkmark"
        }
      ],
      "rewards": []
    },
    {
      "id": "5E80000000000002",
      "title": "A Dedicated LV Line",
      "icon": {
        "id": "modern_industrialization:tin_cable",
        "count": 1
      },
      "x": 3.0,
      "y": 0.0,
      "shape": "circle",
      "size": 1.0,
      "dependencies": [
        "5E80000000000001"
      ],
      "description": [
        "Run tin cable from the turbine output to a small LV workshop. A turbine connects through its marked electrical output face, not every side.",
        "Tin, copper and silver are LV cables in this MI version. Electrum and cupronickel are MV cables; do not substitute them on the LV single-block machine line."
      ],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "5E80000000001020",
          "type": "item",
          "item": {
            "id": "modern_industrialization:tin_cable",
            "count": 1
          },
          "count": 8,
          "consume_items": false
        }
      ],
      "rewards": []
    },
    {
      "id": "5E80000000000003",
      "title": "Watts Before More Machines",
      "icon": {
        "id": "modern_industrialization:lv_steam_turbine",
        "count": 1
      },
      "x": 6.0,
      "y": 0.0,
      "shape": "circle",
      "size": 1.0,
      "dependencies": [
        "5E80000000000002"
      ],
      "description": [
        "One LV Steam Turbine converts up to 32 mB steam per tick into 32 EU/t. Two fully supplied turbines can provide 64 EU/t; empty boilers cannot.",
        "The pinned MI guide gives LV cable networks a 256 EU/t sustained input limit. Single-block electric machines connect to LV cable even when you later unlock more advanced chemistry.",
        "Confirm that a powered machine can run continuously without the steam tank draining. Add boiler and water capacity before adding more loads. The power converter changes energy format; it creates no electricity."
      ],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "5E80000000001030",
          "type": "checkmark"
        }
      ],
      "rewards": []
    },
    {
      "id": "5E80000000000004",
      "title": "Reserve Power in the Hull",
      "icon": {
        "id": "modern_industrialization:redstone_battery",
        "count": 1
      },
      "x": 9.0,
      "y": 0.0,
      "shape": "circle",
      "size": 1.0,
      "dependencies": [
        "5E80000000000003"
      ],
      "description": [
        "Make two Redstone Batteries for one Basic Machine Hull. Before the electric drill, use the pack's starter recipe: three copper plates, two zinc ingots, two redstone and two tin cables per battery.",
        "The native battery-alloy recipe remains available once you have lead and antimony. Those metals come from electric drilling, so the copper/zinc option prevents a hull -> battery -> electric drill -> hull loop."
      ],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "5E80000000001040",
          "type": "item",
          "item": {
            "id": "modern_industrialization:redstone_battery",
            "count": 1
          },
          "count": 2,
          "consume_items": false
        }
      ],
      "rewards": []
    },
    {
      "id": "5E80000000000005",
      "title": "Repeatable Machine Hulls",
      "icon": {
        "id": "modern_industrialization:basic_machine_hull",
        "count": 1
      },
      "x": 12.0,
      "y": 0.0,
      "shape": "hexagon",
      "size": 1.25,
      "dependencies": [
        "5E80000000000004"
      ],
      "description": [
        "A Basic Machine Hull uses a steel machine casing, an Analog Circuit, two Redstone Batteries and three Tin Cables.",
        "The crafting-table route works before your first Assembler. Make one small batch now; later give hulls their own assembly recipe and buffer. The existing turbine already used one hull."
      ],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "5E80000000001050",
          "type": "item",
          "item": {
            "id": "modern_industrialization:basic_machine_hull",
            "count": 1
          },
          "count": 2,
          "consume_items": false
        }
      ],
      "rewards": []
    },
    {
      "id": "5E80000000000006",
      "title": "Expand the Steam Supply",
      "icon": {
        "id": "modern_industrialization:lv_steam_turbine",
        "count": 1
      },
      "x": 15.0,
      "y": 0.0,
      "shape": "diamond",
      "size": 1.0,
      "dependencies": [
        "5E80000000000005"
      ],
      "description": [
        "Keep a steam reserve between generation and consumption, and give water/fuel a renewable input. Use your established steam boiler setup; a Large Steam Boiler is a later optional expansion, not an LV entry requirement.",
        "Add another LV turbine when demand exceeds 32 EU/t. Check steam production, pipe routing and machine buffers before assuming cables are the bottleneck."
      ],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "5E80000000001060",
          "type": "checkmark"
        }
      ],
      "rewards": [],
      "optional": true
    },
    {
